   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "## TPS Cut, Color Match and Paste with a Qwen Image 2.1 edit\n\nCopy `demo_mona_lisa_balloon.webp` from this pack's `example_workflows` folder into ComfyUI's `input` folder (the Mona Lisa, with a rough mask already painted in the sky). To edit somewhere else, paint your own mask: right-click the Load Image node, Open in MaskEditor.\n\n1. **TPS Cut** cuts the masked area out and enlarges it, so only the cut goes through VAE and sampler.\n2. **Qwen Image 2.1** edits the cut.\n3. **TPS Color Match** undoes what the edit changed everywhere: the whole cut comes back darker, with its texture redrawn. It measures that only where the edit left the picture alone, so the balloon keeps its own color. **measure_view** shows where it measured, the plateau before and after and the grade it fitted; **change_mask** is what it took as changed. Bypass the node (Ctrl+B) to see the edit unmatched.\n4. **TPS Paste** lines the cut up with the original (`align` full: Qwen Image 2.1 shifts the picture by a few pixels) and blends it back. Outside the mask nothing changes.\n\n**When the change mask is wrong.** An edit that redraws the texture around the object (a lantern that relights the wall) can flood the change mask. Paint the object yourself, or take it from a segmentation node, and wire it to Color Match's `change_mask`, at the size of the source or of the cut. Light the object casts past your mask is still found.\n\n**Settings.** TPS Cut `size_multiple` 32 and the encoder's `resolution` 0 keep the cut at its own size. The text encoder is `qwen3vl_8b_int8_convrot`, with no prompt enhancer; cfg 1, so the negative prompt does nothing.\n\nMona Lisa, Leonardo da Vinci, public domain.\n"
   ],
   "title": "Read me"
  }
 ],
